course: dictionary
lesson: 9393
title: Words that bounce
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how something moves or feels. Springy is one of them. Something springy bounces back to its shape after you press, squash or stretch it, like a spring. «Red kangaroos hop with springy tendons that store energy.» The tendons spring back, so the kangaroo can hop with very little effort.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «Every evening an orangutan bends branches into a springy platform» tells you the orangutan is making a bed, so the platform must be firm but give a little and spring back. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then swap in your meaning, bouncy, and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Springy can also describe how someone walks. A springy step is light, quick and full of energy, so the walker is probably happy or excited. A kangaroo is a living pogo stick, bouncing along fast with hardly any effort.
fact: Springy means bouncy: it goes back to its shape after you press, squash or stretch it.
fact: A springy walk or step is light, quick and full of energy.
fact: Springy is an adjective, so it can change: springy, springier, springiest.
fact: In science, springy materials such as rubber, sponge and coiled metal come back to shape.
fact: In cooking, a cake is done when its top feels springy.
exercise: «Red kangaroos hop with springy tendons.» What does springy mean here? | Loud and noisy | Very heavy | Wet and muddy | *Bouncy, going back to its shape
exercise: «The walker had a springy step as she headed home.» What does springy suggest? | Frozen with cold | Slow and tired | Angry and stamping | *Light, quick and full of energy
exercise: «The sponge was soft and springy, and it sprang back when Sam pressed it.» Find and copy the word that means bouncy. | pressed | sponge | *springy | sprang
test: Which of these is a springy material that comes back to its shape? | *Rubber | Sand | Ice | Wet paper
test: «A kangaroo hops fast with springy tendons that store energy.» Why does this cost the kangaroo little effort? | It hops only downhill | It runs on wheels | It is too lazy to walk | *Its springy tendons store energy at each landing
exam: Mia says springy means soft and sticky. What is the best answer? | Sleepy and slow | Soft and sticky, like toffee | *Bouncy, going back to its shape after you press it | Cold and hard like stone
